+# Deploy-lane RCA for #1819/#1838 — green builds are not the fix; new images fail at boot
+
+**Discovered:** 2026-10-28 00:48-01:12Z, while executing the loop-assigned work order #1838 (zai-cron-agent-loop, zero-credential MCP-tower agent; atomic claim `work_claim` GRANT_NEW at 01:00:55Z, renewed to 01:35Z).
+
+## Executive finding
+
+Work order #1838 proved the build layer is fixed. This RCA completes the chain: **the deploy swap does not stall on infra — the NEW container fails to serve, and Render marks the deploy `update_failed` after boot retries.** Reproduced deterministically live: two consecutive clean builds (23:19Z and 01:02Z) both flipped to `update_failed` within ~90 seconds of image export.
+
+## Live status transitions (tower `render_service_health`, service IDs in artifacts)
+
+| Service | 00:10Z (WO filed) | 01:05Z | 01:04Z (post-redeploy) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| render-primary `srv-dau7c9ek1f9s73almn0g` | update_failed | build_in_progress | **update_failed again** |
+| render-worker `srv-dabm7evqj5pc738jkf30` | update_failed | build_in_progress | **update_failed again** |
+| render-api `srv-dbappass728c7396p580` | update_failed | update_failed (untouched) | update_failed (no retry since 23:37Z) |
+
+## Boot-phase evidence (tower `render_get_logs`, type=app, window 01:01:30-01:06:00Z)
+
+1. **render-worker (hard crash, cleanest signal):** the new container boots the ASGI server with the module reference `worker:app` and dies instantly with `ERROR: Error loading ASGI app. Could not import module "worker"`. The monorepo restructure moved/renamed the worker entrypoint; the start command still expects a top-level `worker` module that no longer exists in the image. Boot retry loop ends in `update_failed`.
+2. **render-primary (partial boot, then terminated during swap):** new container logs a pydantic plugin `ImportError` warning — `cannot import name 'settings' from partially initialized module 'core.config'` (circular import, core/config.py ↔ plugin loader). It then logs `[VAULT] Generated new Master Key at /root/.supremeai_vault/vault.key` — **the vault master key is regenerated per boot on ephemeral container storage** (data-plane hazard: anything encrypted under the previous key becomes unreadable after redeploy). The container reaches `Application startup complete`, answers `/health/live` 200 at 01:02:58Z, and Render terminates it at 01:03:04Z during the swap; final status `update_failed`.
+3. **render-api (silent, stuck):** last build attempt 23:28-23:37Z ended cleanly at image export; build log window 23:45Z-01:10Z is EMPTY — Render never auto-retries a failed swap, and no new commit has re-triggered autoDeploy. `healthCheckPath` is empty, so boot failures on this service surface only as the generic swap failure with no health-check signal.
+
+## Causality chain (updates #1838's chain, steps 5-6 resolved)
+
+Pre-fix Dockerfile errors (fixed by #1780/#1794) → green builds, clean image export ✔ → **deploy swap invokes the new image → new image fails boot/serving (worker: missing module; primary: circular import + per-boot vault keygen; api: unverifiable, no health check path) → Render retries boot, then marks `update_failed` → no auto-retry → node keeps serving the pre-fix container** (public gateway still missing #1728 security headers, matching #1819 drift byte-for-byte).
+
+## Impact
+
+- Every monorepo merge since ≤2026-10-24 is absent from all three nodes; #1728 headers, #1729 fleet-status auth, #1772→#1806 hardening all absent from live traffic.
+- New regression class exposed: the fixed Dockerfiles now produce images whose *runtime* is broken by the monorepo restructure — CI stays green because Render deploys post-merge, outside GH Actions.
+- Vault master-key regeneration per boot is a data-integrity hazard independent of the deploy lane.
+
+## Recommended fixes (smallest first, owner lane)
+
+1. **worker (supremeai-core):** align the service start command with the post-restructure module path (or add a thin `worker.py` entrypoint shim at repo root that re-exports the app). One-file change; unblocks the worker swap.
+2. **primary (supremeai-core):** break the `core.config` circular import (defer the plugin load that imports settings during module init); load the vault master key from persistent storage/env instead of generating a new one per boot.
+3. **api (supremeai-api):** set a real `healthCheckPath` (e.g. `/healthz` exists and returns 200) so boot failures present as health-check failures with visible logs.
+4. **Admin lane after 1-3 land:** trigger Clear build cache & deploy once per service — deploys do not auto-retry; the three fixes are runtime code/config, not Dockerfile (respecting #1838's never-do register: no new Dockerfile PRs).
+5. **Guard proposal:** post-merge deploy probe — if `deploys[0].status != live` within N minutes of a push, open an ops issue automatically; closes the Green-CI blind spot permanently.
+
